---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — LaunchPad"
  description="LaunchPad collects no personal data: no accounts, no sign-up, no tracking cookies, no third-party trackers."
  path=""
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container column">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Short version: LaunchPad collects nothing about you.</p>

      <h2>No account, no sign-up</h2>
      <p>
        There is nothing to register for. The site has no login, no email capture, and no
        contact form. If you want to reach the project, use the email address on the
        <a href={`${base}/about`}>About page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Nothing you type is sent anywhere</h2>
      <p>
        The calculators run entirely in your browser. The numbers you enter never leave your
        device and are never stored on a server, because there is no server — this is a set
        of static files.
      </p>

      <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
      <p>
        Your chosen currency is saved in your browser's local storage so you do not have to
        pick it again. That stays on your device, is not readable by the project, and
        clearing your browser data removes it.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and trackers</h2>
      <p>
        LaunchPad sets no cookies. There is no Google Analytics, no advertising pixel, and
        no social media tracker. Fonts are served from this site rather than a font CDN, so
        loading a page does not tell any third party that you were here.
      </p>

      <h2>If analytics are added later</h2>
      <p>
        Any future analytics will be cookieless and aggregate-only — counts of pages read
        and calculators used, with no profile of individual visitors. This page will be
        updated before that happens.
      </p>

      <h2>Age</h2>
      <p>
        LaunchPad is written for people aged 15 to 21, and collecting no personal data is a
        deliberate choice: it means the site does not need parental consent handling under
        India's DPDP rules, the EU's GDPR, or the US COPPA.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lede { font-size: 19px; color: var(--ink-2); }
</style>
